      "problem": "Consider a linear transformation $T:{R}^{10}\\to {R}^{10}.$ If $\\text{rank}(T)=6$ then $\\text{nullity}(T)=$",
      "worked_solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $T:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{n},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)+\\text{nullity}(T)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given transformation, we have $n=10.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(T)+\\text{nullity}(T) & =n \\\\ 6+\\text{nullity}(T) & =10 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(T) & =10-6 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
